  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 129 AM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nPatchy early morning fog will be possible again today, but it should \nbe mainly near rivers and lakes. \n\nA large upper ridge to our west will gradually shift eastward during \nthe period and surface high pressure to our north and northeast will \nextend into our area, keeping our weather dry into early next week. \nModels suggest the upper ridge may break down and some models have a \nfront approaching by mid week, but even then moisture looks very \nlimited and thus we have a dry forecast for the entire period \nthrough Wednesday. \n\nFor the entire period we can expect cool nights and pleasant \nafternoons with high temperatures each day not far either side of \nseasonal normals. We will also see low relative humidity values \nduring the afternoon hours.",
